RPi ALERT release signing -- the PUBLIC key goes here (Ed25519, SPKI PEM).

PLACEHOLDER: no key is configured yet, so rpi-alert-update installs releases
WITHOUT verifying them, exactly as it always has. This file deliberately does
not contain a key.

To turn verification on, replace this whole file with your Ed25519 public key
in PEM form (the block whose header line starts with five dashes, the words
PUBLIC KEY, and five more dashes). From then on the updater verifies every
release against it and refuses one it cannot.

See docs/release-signing.md for the one-time setup (generate the key, add the
private half as the RELEASE_SIGNING_KEY Actions secret, commit the public half
here) and the rollout order.
